From: SM-G955N Ubuntu port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: fimc-is2: report queue capabilities and reject empty enums

Native V4L2 queries expose missing device_caps, incorrect capture direction
on output ports and ENUM_FMT callbacks that return success without setting
any format. Fill caps from the registered queue ioctls and return EINVAL for
these unimplemented enumeration callbacks. Do not invent working capture or
format support and do not suppress V4L2 core warnings. Android camera HAL
streaming remains separate work.

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-video-ssvc1.c b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-video-ssvc1.c
--- a/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-video-ssvc1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/exynos/fimc-is2/fimc-is-video-ssvc1.c
@@ -258,15 +258,14 @@
 static int fimc_is_ssxvc1_video_querycap(struct file *file, void *fh,
 	struct v4l2_capability *cap)
 {
-	/* Todo : add to query capability code */
-	return 0;
+	return fimc_is_video_querycap(file, cap);
 }
 
 static int fimc_is_ssxvc1_video_enum_fmt_mplane(struct file *file, void *priv,
 	struct v4l2_fmtdesc *f)
 {
-	dbg("%s\n", __func__);
-	return 0;
+	/* No format description is implemented for this private pipeline port. */
+	return -EINVAL;
 }
 
 static int fimc_is_ssxvc1_video_get_format_mplane(struct file *file, void *fh,
